  "scope": {
    "project": "ripple",
    "scope": "compact",
    "implemented": [
      "Custom New board (title, question, 1-5 allowlisted URLs, requirements) and editable example inputs; optional bounded Telem source discovery",
      "Real server-side Telem search/fetch with host allowlist, URL safety checks, per-result status and canonical-URL recheck",
      "Model fact extraction requiring literal source quotes; unverifiable facts stay unknown, cross-source same-key different values become conflicting",
      "Source -> fact -> answer DAG with typed semantic hashes, cycle/dangling/duplicate/40-node checks, reverse-closure invalidation and model-proposed (reviewable) dependencies",
      "Requirement edit recomputes only affected answers without source acquisition and is labeled requirements_edit, not an external change",
      "Refresh re-reads sources with no_cache; unchanged facts reuse answers; failed/partial reads keep last values and mark dependents unknown",
      "HMAC-signed board snapshots with expiry, verified before quota",
      "Browser IndexedDB library with immutable revisions, expected-revision writes, export/import (imports unverified) and delete",
      "Same-origin guard, body caps, strict schemas, signed visitor cookie, Upstash atomic quotas, kill switch",
      "Legacy /api/refresh evaluation adapter with paired baseline (refresh-all) and treatment (affected closure) strategies; fixture mode localhost-only behind ALLOW_FIXTURE_MODE",
      "Client-only Simulation Lab labeled SYNTHETIC FIXTURE / mode=fixture",
      "/privacy and /integrations pages; /api/health readiness",
      "Local Node stdio MCP kit with nine tools, two portable skills, project-scoped setup helper, private per-origin vault and real downloadable source archive/checksum; same public API and quota boundary",
      "Direct Tavily basic extraction supplies evidence text and refresh observations in create/refresh/legacy routes; additive extractor/request/status and per-batch usage/attempt trace with labeled degraded Telem fallback"
    ],
